/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 126 0 R
/T (At position i = 2 the digit 6 is non-zero, contributing prev1 = 2, and the pair 26 is valid, contributing prev2 = 1. Consequently current = 2 + 1 = 3. The loop ends and prev1 = 3 is returned, which is precisely the expected output Ways = 3. The two contributions correspond exactly to the decodings obtained by appending F to BB and V, and to the decoding obtained by appending Z to B.)
/E (At position i = 2 the digit 6 is non-zero, contributing prev1 = 2, and the pair 26 is valid, contributing prev2 = 1. Consequently current = 2 + 1 = 3. The loop ends and prev1 = 3 is returned, which is precisely the expected output Ways = 3. The two contributions correspond exactly to the decodings obtained by appending F to BB and V, and to the decoding obtained by appending Z to B.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
