430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 130 0 R
/T (A leading zero or an empty string is rejected before the loop begins, so 06 and "" return 0 immediately. An internal zero is never counted by the single-digit branch; it can only contribute through the two-digit branch as 10 or 20, which is why 10 and 201 return 1 while 100 returns 0, the trailing zero having no valid partner. A pair greater than 26 is filtered by the upper bound of the range test, as seen in 27. A single-character input skips the loop entirely and returns the initial value 1. These behaviours cover the normal, boundary and hidden test categories expected by the Test Case Handling criterion.)
/E (A leading zero or an empty string is rejected before the loop begins, so 06 and "" return 0 immediately. An internal zero is never counted by the single-digit branch; it can only contribute through the two-digit branch as 10 or 20, which is why 10 and 201 return 1 while 100 returns 0, the trailing zero having no valid partner. A pair greater than 26 is filtered by the upper bound of the range test, as seen in 27. A single-character input skips the loop entirely and returns the initial value 1. These behaviours cover the normal, boundary and hidden test categories expected by the Test Case Handling criterion.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
