/T (For the core DP counting algorithm the space complexity is O\(1\), because the function stores only the three scalar variables prev2, prev1 and current, together with the temporary two_digit, instead of maintaining an entire DP array of length n + 1. This optimisation is possible because the recurrence refers only to the two immediately preceding states.)
/E (For the core DP counting algorithm the space complexity is O\(1\), because the function stores only the three scalar variables prev2, prev1 and current, together with the temporary two_digit, instead of maintaining an entire DP array of length n + 1. This optimisation is possible because the recurrence refers only to the two immediately preceding states.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
