/Title (A leading zero or an empty string is rejected before the loop begins, so 06 and "" return 0 immediately. An internal zero is never counted by the single-digit branch; it can only contribute through the two-digit branch as 10 or 20, which is why 10 and 201 return 1 while 100 returns 0, the trailing zero having no valid partner. A pair greater than 26 is filtered by the upper bound of the range test, as seen in 27. A single-character input skips the loop entirely and returns the initial value 1. These behaviours cover the normal, boundary and hidden test categories expected by the Test Case Handling criterion.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 822 0 R
/First 979 0 R
/Last 980 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
908 0 obj
<<
/Title (For the core DP counting algorithm the space complexity is O\(1\), because the function stores only the three scalar variables prev2, prev1 and current, together with the temporary two_digit, instead of maintaining an entire DP array of length n + 1. This optimisation is possible because the recurrence refers only to the two immediately preceding states.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 824 0 R
/Next 981 0 R
>>
