/Title (The string 226 is scanned from left to right. The first digit 2 must be taken alone as B, or combined with the second digit. If the first two digits are taken separately, the remaining digits 2 and 6 may either be split into B and F, giving BBF, or joined as the pair 26, which is valid and gives BZ. If instead the first two digits are joined as the pair 22, which is valid and equals V, the only digit left is 6, which must be taken alone as F, giving VF. Every branch of this reasoning has been exhausted, so exactly three decodings exist.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 897 0 R
/Next 959 0 R
>>
endobj
959 0 obj
