/Title (Any decoding of a three-digit string must partition it into blocks of size one or two, and only three such partitions exist: \(1,1,1\), \(2,1\) and \(1,2\). The partition \(3\) is impossible because 226 exceeds 26. All three admissible partitions were tested above and all three happened to be valid, since 22 and 26 both lie within the permitted range and no digit of the string is zero. Therefore the count of valid decodings is exactly 3, which matches the value returned by the Dynamic Programming function.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 903 0 R
/First 1022 0 R
/Last 1023 0 R
/Count -2
>>
